<!-- ============ SECTION 2 · WHY ============ -->
<section id="why">
  <div class="sec-head">
    <span class="eyebrow rv">Section 02 · The why</span>
    <h2 class="rv">Why BZmail <span class="grad">exists</span></h2>
    <p class="lead rv">One Gmail account can’t run real email marketing. BZmail was designed as three connected surfaces — engine, admin room and user panel — so owners, teams and customers each get exactly what they need.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="duo-grid">
    <div class="duo rv" data-num="01"><span class="ptag">WHY THE ENGINE</span>
      <h3>Gmail’s hard sending caps</h3>
      <div class="prob"><b>THE PROBLEM</b>Gmail caps every free account at ~500 emails/day, then blocks it. A single sender can never scale a real campaign.</div>
      <div class="fix"><b>THE BZMAIL FIX</b>A rotating pool of Gmail SMTP servers (smtp.gmail.com : 587) with per-server Active toggles and instant failover — volume now has no ceiling.</div>
      <span class="arrow">↓</span>
    </div>
    <div class="duo rv" data-num="02"><span class="ptag">WHY THE ADMIN PANEL</span>
      <h3>Owners were flying blind</h3>
      <div class="prob"><b>THE PROBLEM</b>Spreadsheets, scattered scripts and separate tools — zero visibility over users, servers, campaigns and results.</div>
      <div class="fix"><b>THE BZMAIL FIX</b>One admin control room: users, guests, servers, projects, campaigns, templates, live analytics and Copy / Excel / PDF exports.</div>
      <span class="arrow">↓</span>
    </div>
    <div class="duo rv" data-num="03"><span class="ptag">WHY THE USER PANEL (PWA)</span>
      <h3>Customers on any device</h3>
      <div class="prob"><b>THE PROBLEM</b>End-users needed access from any phone with no app-store installs and no clunky legacy interfaces.</div>
      <div class="fix"><b>THE BZMAIL FIX</b>An installable PWA with guest login &amp; registration and a high-UX, iconic dark-glass interface that feels native everywhere.</div>
      <span class="arrow">↓</span>
    </div>
    <div class="duo rv" data-num="04"><span class="ptag">WHY THE IMPACT</span>
      <h3>Sending blind burns domains</h3>
      <div class="prob"><b>THE PROBLEM</b>No opens, no clicks, no bounce data — lists decay, reputations burn, money disappears.</div>
      <div class="fix"><b>THE BZMAIL FIX</b>Real tracking on everything: open / click / bounce rates, fail-lists and don’t-try lists keep campaigns measurable and domains safe.</div>
      <span class="arrow">↓</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="flow-wrap rv">
    <div class="flow">
      <div class="fnode"><h4>📨 Campaign queue</h4><p>Templates + email groups ready to fire</p></div>
      <div class="fpipe"></div>
